(PredictIQ: Hackathon Jury Defense Guide \(Part 1 - ML & Physics\)) Tj
0 -26 Td
/F2 12 Tf
0 -20 Td
(CATEGORY 1: MACHINE LEARNING & MODELING DEFENSE) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -16 Td
(Q1: Why use an Autoencoder for Stage 1 instead of standard One-Class SVM or Isolation Forest?) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(A: Industrial sensor degradation is multi-dimensional and continuous. Isolation Forests create rigid,) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(step-function partition boundaries that fail to capture smooth physical wear. An Autoencoder models) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(the non-linear correlations between sensors. Reconstruction MSE provides a smooth, physical) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Health Index that smoothly tracks clearance erosion and thermodynamic loss.) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -16 Td
(Q2: Why did you pick GRU/LSTM over Transformers for Remaining Useful Life \(RUL\)?) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(A: Industrial edge hardware \(PLC / FADEC\) has strict memory and latency bounds. For sequential) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(window sizes of 30 cycles, self-attention mechanisms in Transformers introduce quadratic O\(N^2\)) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(overhead and overfit on small fleets without providing measurable accuracy gains. GRUs converge in) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(under 2.5 seconds on CPU with high inference speed \(<2ms/window\).) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -16 Td
(Q3: Why is RUL clipped at 125 cycles in the training pipeline?) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(A: In turbomachinery, brand-new components do not exhibit measurable wear during early cycles.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Labeling an engine at cycle 5 with an RUL of 190 forces the neural network to learn an unobservable) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(linear decay slope. Piecewise linear clipping \(cap = 125\) reflects the physical reality that wear) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(only manifests after the operational baseline.) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -16 Td
(Q4: Explain the NASA C-MAPSS Asymmetric Scoring metric and why MSE is dangerous in aerospace.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(A: Symmetric MSE treats predicting 10 cycles too late identically to 10 cycles early. In aviation,) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(predicting late \(d > 0\) means an engine fails in-flight before maintenance is scheduled! NASA penalty) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(penalizes late calls exponentially \(s = exp\(d/13\)-1\) much harsher than early calls \(s = exp\(-d/10\)-1\).) Tj
ET
endstream
